{"format":"vetro-plugin","version":1,"manifest":{"id":"bedtime","name":"Bedtime","version":"1.0.0","apiVersion":1,"permissions":["exec"],"main":"index.js","ui":{"label":"Bedtime"},"description":"Turn the TV off at set times or after a sleep timer, or open an app on a schedule. No network.","author":"piecifra"},"files":{"README.md":"# Bedtime\n\nTurn the TV off at set times or after a sleep timer, or open an app on a schedule. A **Bedtime** tab lists the\nrules with their next run, sets a sleep timer (15, 30, 60 or 90 minutes) and shows the last actions.\n\n- A rule is a time, one or more days of the week, and an action: **turn the TV off** or **open an app** (picked from\n  the installed apps). Up to 20 rules.\n- Times are the TV's local time. A rule runs once a day, within two minutes of its time; a time missed while the TV\n  was off is skipped, never caught up later. When an app and power off are due in the same minute, the app opens first.\n- The sleep timer is saved, so it survives a restart of Vetro.\n- Rules run only while this Shard is switched on. Opening an app needs the TV on.\n- **Test now** runs the chosen action at once. Turning the TV off needs a second click (the page cannot show dialogs).\n- **Reset Bedtime** (second click to confirm) deletes every rule, cancels the sleep timer and clears the last\n  actions.\n\n## Permissions\n\n`exec`: turning the TV off and opening an app go through the TV's own tools, as root.\n\n## Commands it runs\n\n| Command | When | Why |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `/usr/bin/input_keyevent XF86PowerOff` | a rule with \"Turn the TV off\" is due, the sleep timer ends, or **Test now** | the TV's discrete power-off key (never a toggle), the same command Vetro's own TV controls use |\n| `app_launcher -s <appId>` | a rule with \"Open an app\" is due, or **Test now** | open the app; `<appId>` must be a Tizen app id (letters, digits, `.` `_` `-`) and is checked before use |\n| `app_launcher -l` | the page asks for the app list (cached 5 minutes) | names and ids for the app picker |\n\nNothing runs at start or on its own except these, at the times you set.\n\n## Network\n\nNone.\n\n## Data it keeps\n\nIts own `config.json` on the TV: the rules, the sleep timer's end time, the date each rule last ran (so it runs once\na day), and the last 20 actions with their result (time, what, done or the error). **Reset Bedtime** empties it;\nremoving the Shard deletes it.\n\n## Tested\n\nSamsung QE43Q60BAUXXN (Q60B, 2022, firmware T-NKLBDEUC-1720.7), Tizen 6.5, kernel 5.4, ARMv7, Vetro 0.5.0,\ninstalled from a file. **Other models are untested.**\n\n- Power off by a rule: the TV turned off at the rule's time (logged as done). Opening an app with **Test now**: the\n  TV's Internet browser (`org.tizen.browser`) opened (logged as done). The app picker lists the TV's 411 apps; rules,\n  the sleep timer and **Reset Bedtime** through the Shard's routes.\n- Off the TV: rules and their validation, the local-time schedule (once a day, the two-minute window, no catch-up),\n  the sleep timer across a reload, app before power off, failures logged, reset, and the app list parsed from that TV's real\n  `app_launcher -l` output.\n","index.js":"'use strict';\n// Bedtime: turn the TV off at set times or after a sleep timer, or open an app on a schedule.\n// Commands (through ctx.execute, as root), the same ones Vetro itself uses:\n//   /usr/bin/input_keyevent XF86PowerOff   a discrete \"power off\" key, never a toggle\n//   app_launcher -s <appId>                open an app (the id is validated)\n//   app_launcher -l                        list the installed apps, for the picker\n// A rule fires at most once a day, within two minutes of its time; a time missed while the TV was off is not caught\n// up later. The schedule uses the TV's local time. Plain ES5: older TVs run Node 4.4.\nvar fs = require('fs'), path = require('path');\nvar TICK_MS = 15000, WINDOW_MIN = 2, MAX_RULES = 20, MAX_LOG = 20, MAX_BODY = 16384, APPS_CACHE_MS = 300000;\nvar APP_ID = /^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]{0,127}$/, TIME = /^([01]\\d|2[0-3]):([0-5]\\d)$/, RULE_ID = /^[a-z0-9]{1,16}$/;\nvar OFF = '/usr/bin/input_keyevent XF86PowerOff';\n\nfunction pad(n) { return (n < 10 ? '0' : '') + n; }\nfunction dayKey(d) { return d.getFullYear() + '-' + pad(d.getMonth() + 1) + '-' + pad(d.getDate()); }\n\n// Returns a clean rule or throws. days: 0 = Sunday … 6 = Saturday, as Date#getDay.\nfunction validRule(r, i) {\n    if (!r || typeof r !== 'object') throw new Error('Rule ' + (i + 1) + ' is not an object');\n    var out = { id: RULE_ID.test(r.id || '') ? r.id : Math.random().toString(36).slice(2, 10), enabled: r.enabled !== false };\n    if (!TIME.test(r.time || '')) throw new Error('Rule ' + (i + 1) + ': time must be HH:MM');\n    out.time = r.time;\n    if (!Array.isArray(r.days) || !r.days.length) throw new Error('Rule ' + (i + 1) + ': pick at least one day');\n    var days = [];\n    r.days.forEach(function (d) { if (d !== Math.floor(d) || d < 0 || d > 6) throw new Error('Rule ' + (i + 1) + ': invalid day'); if (days.indexOf(d) < 0) days.push(d); });\n    out.days = days.sort();\n    if (r.action === 'off') out.action = 'off';\n    else if (r.action === 'launch') {\n        if (!APP_ID.test(r.appId || '')) throw new Error('Rule ' + (i + 1) + ': invalid app');\n        out.action = 'launch'; out.appId = r.appId;\n        if (typeof r.appName === 'string') out.appName = r.appName.slice(0, 60);\n    } else throw new Error('Rule ' + (i + 1) + ': action must be off or launch');\n    return out;\n}\nfunction validRules(list) {\n    if (!Array.isArray(list)) throw new Error('rules must be a list');\n    if (list.length > MAX_RULES) throw new Error('At most ' + MAX_RULES + ' rules');\n    return list.map(validRule);\n}\n\n// Which rules are due now: enabled, today is one of its days, now is within WINDOW_MIN minutes after its time, and\n// it has not fired today.\nfunction due(rules, lastFired, now) {\n    var d = new Date(now), minutes = d.getHours() * 60 + d.getMinutes(), today = dayKey(d);\n    return rules.filter(function (r) {\n        if (!r.enabled || r.days.indexOf(d.getDay()) < 0 || lastFired[r.id] === today) return false;\n        var m = TIME.exec(r.time), at = Number(m[1]) * 60 + Number(m[2]);\n        return minutes >= at && minutes < at + WINDOW_MIN;\n    });\n}\n\n// The next time each rule fires, for the page (searches the next 8 days).\nfunction nextRun(r, now) {\n    if (!r.enabled) return null;\n    var m = TIME.exec(r.time);\n    for (var i = 0; i < 8; i++) {\n        var d = new Date(now); d.setDate(d.getDate() + i); d.setHours(Number(m[1]), Number(m[2]), 0, 0);\n        if (r.days.indexOf(d.getDay()) >= 0 && d.getTime() > now - WINDOW_MIN * 60000) return d.getTime();\n    }\n    return null;\n}\n\nfunction command(action) { return action.action === 'off' ? OFF : 'app_launcher -s ' + action.appId; }\n\nfunction parseApps(out) {\n    var apps = [], seen = {};\n    String(out || '').split('\\n').forEach(function (line) {\n        var m = /^\\s*'([^']*)'\\s+'([^']+)'\\s*$/.exec(line);\n        if (m && APP_ID.test(m[2]) && !seen[m[2]]) { seen[m[2]] = true; apps.push({ name: m[1], appId: m[2] }); }\n    });\n    return apps.sort(function (a, b) { return a.name.toLowerCase() < b.name.toLowerCase() ? -1 : 1; });\n}\n\nfunction json(res, body, code) {\n    res.writeHead(code || 200, { 'content-type': 'application/json', 'cache-control': 'no-store' });\n    res.end(JSON.stringify(body));\n}\nfunction readJson(req, cb) {\n    var chunks = [], size = 0, done = false;\n    req.on('data', function (c) { size += c.length; if (size > MAX_BODY) { if (!done) { done = true; cb(new Error('Request too large')); } return; } chunks.push(c); });\n    req.on('end', function () { if (done) return; done = true; var p; try { p = JSON.parse(Buffer.concat(chunks).toString('utf8') || '{}'); } catch (e) { return cb(new Error('Invalid JSON')); } if (!p || typeof p !== 'object' || Array.isArray(p)) return cb(new Error('Invalid JSON')); cb(null, p); });\n    req.on('error', function (e) { if (!done) { done = true; cb(e); } });\n}\n// The page ships next to this file; a test harness may give an empty ctx.dir. start() never fails over it.\nfunction loadPage(ctx) {\n    var places = [path.join(__dirname, 'ui.html'), path.join(ctx.dir || '', 'ui.html')];\n    for (var i = 0; i < places.length; i++) { try { return fs.readFileSync(places[i], 'utf8'); } catch (e) { /* next */ } }\n    return '<!doctype html><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><p>Page file missing: reinstall this Shard.</p>';\n}\n\nmodule.exports = function (ctx, deps) {\n    deps = deps || {};\n    var clock = deps.now || function () { return Date.now(); };\n    var timer = null, page = null, apps = null, appsAt = 0, running = false;\n    // config.json: { rules: [...], sleepAt: ms or null, lastFired: { ruleId: 'YYYY-MM-DD' }, log: [...] }\n    function load() { try { var c = ctx.config.get(); return c && typeof c === 'object' && !Array.isArray(c) ? c : {}; } catch (e) { return {}; } }\n    function save(c) { try { ctx.config.set(c); return true; } catch (e) { return false; } }\n    function rules(c) { try { return validRules(c.rules || []); } catch (e) { return []; } }\n    function log(c, entry) { c.log = (Array.isArray(c.log) ? c.log : []).concat([entry]).slice(-MAX_LOG); }\n    function act(action, why) {\n        return ctx.execute(command(action), 15000).then(function (r) {\n            return { ok: r.exit_code === 0 && !r.timed_out, error: r.exit_code === 0 ? null : String(r.stderr || r.stdout || 'exit ' + r.exit_code).trim().slice(0, 200) };\n        }, function (e) { return { ok: false, error: String(e && e.message || e) }; }).then(function (res) {\n            var c = load();\n            log(c, { at: clock(), why: why, action: action.action, appId: action.appId || null, ok: res.ok, error: res.error });\n            save(c);\n            return res;\n        });\n    }\n    function tick() {\n        if (running) return;\n        var c = load(), now = clock(), work = [];\n        if (typeof c.sleepAt === 'number' && now >= c.sleepAt) {\n            c.sleepAt = null; save(c);\n            work.push([{ action: 'off' }, 'sleep timer']);\n        }\n        var list = due(rules(c), c.lastFired || {}, now);\n        if (list.length) {\n            c = load(); c.lastFired = c.lastFired || {};\n            list.forEach(function (r) { c.lastFired[r.id] = dayKey(new Date(now)); });\n            save(c);\n            // App launches before power off when both are due in the same minute.\n            list.sort(function (a, b) { return (a.action === 'off') - (b.action === 'off'); });\n            list.forEach(function (r) { work.push([r, 'rule ' + r.time]); });\n        }\n        if (!work.length) return;\n        running = true;\n        work.reduce(function (p, w) { return p.then(function () { return act(w[0], w[1]); }); }, Promise.resolve())\n            .then(function () { running = false; }, function () { running = false; });\n    }\n    function state() {\n        var c = load(), now = clock(), list = rules(c), d = new Date(now);\n        return {\n            now: now, tzOffsetMinutes: -d.getTimezoneOffset(),\n            rules: list.map(function (r) { var o = JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(r)); o.next = nextRun(r, now); return o; }),\n            sleepAt: typeof c.sleepAt === 'number' && c.sleepAt > now ? c.sleepAt : null,\n            log: (Array.isArray(c.log) ? c.log : []).slice().reverse()\n        };\n    }\n    function listApps() {\n        if (apps && clock() - appsAt < APPS_CACHE_MS) return Promise.resolve(apps);\n        return ctx.execute('app_launcher -l', 20000).then(function (r) {\n            var list = parseApps(r.stdout);\n            if (!list.length) throw new Error('App list unavailable');\n            apps = list; appsAt = clock(); return list;\n        });\n    }\n    return {\n        start: function () { page = loadPage(ctx); timer = (deps.every || setInterval)(tick, TICK_MS); if (timer && timer.unref) timer.unref(); },\n        stop: function () { (deps.clear || clearInterval)(timer); timer = null; page = null; },\n        status: function () { var s = state(); return { rules: s.rules.length, sleepAt: s.sleepAt }; },\n        route: function (req, res, sub) {\n            if (sub === 'ui' && req.method === 'GET') { res.writeHead(200, { 'content-type': 'text/html; charset=utf-8', 'cache-control': 'no-store' }); res.end(page || ''); return true; }\n            if (sub === 'state' && req.method === 'GET') { json(res, state()); return true; }\n            if (sub === 'apps' && req.method === 'GET') { listApps().then(function (l) { json(res, { apps: l }); }, function (e) { json(res, { ok: false, error: e.message }, 503); }); return true; }\n            if (req.method !== 'POST' || ['rules', 'sleep', 'run', 'reset'].indexOf(sub) < 0) return false;\n            readJson(req, function (err, p) {\n                if (err) return json(res, { ok: false, error: err.message }, 400);\n                if (sub === 'reset') {\n                    // Back to a fresh install: no rules, no sleep timer, no history.\n                    if (!save({})) return json(res, { ok: false, error: 'Reset could not be saved' }, 500);\n                    return json(res, state());\n                }\n                var c = load();\n                if (sub === 'rules') {\n                    try { c.rules = validRules(p.rules); } catch (e) { return json(res, { ok: false, error: e.message }, 400); }\n                    // Saving does not make an edited rule fire again today if its new time already passed.\n                    if (!save(c)) return json(res, { ok: false, error: 'Rules could not be saved' }, 500);\n                    return json(res, state());\n                }\n                if (sub === 'sleep') {\n                    if (p.minutes === null) c.sleepAt = null;\n                    else if (p.minutes === Math.floor(p.minutes) && p.minutes >= 1 && p.minutes <= 600) c.sleepAt = clock() + p.minutes * 60000;\n                    else return json(res, { ok: false, error: 'minutes must be 1–600, or null to cancel' }, 400);\n                    if (!save(c)) return json(res, { ok: false, error: 'Sleep timer could not be saved' }, 500);\n                    return json(res, state());\n                }\n                // run: try an action now from the page (\"Test\")\n                var action;\n                try { action = validRule({ time: '00:00', days: [0], action: p.action, appId: p.appId }, 0); } catch (e) { return json(res, { ok: false, error: e.message }, 400); }\n                act(action, 'test').then(function (r) { json(res, { ok: r.ok, error: r.error, state: state() }, r.ok ? 200 : 502); });\n            });\n            return true;\n        }\n    };\n};\nmodule.exports.validRules = validRules;\nmodule.exports.due = due;\nmodule.exports.nextRun = nextRun;\nmodule.exports.parseApps = parseApps;\nmodule.exports.command = command;\nmodule.exports.OFF = OFF;\n","ui.html":"<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width,initial-scale=1\">\n<meta name=\"color-scheme\" content=\"light dark\"><title>Bedtime</title>\n<style>\n:root{--bg:#080f23;--surface:#101c35;--raised:#192943;--border:#344360;--text:#f5f8ff;--muted:#aab8d1;--action:#123bb5;--ok:#7fcba0;--bad:#ef8a80}\n@media (prefers-color-scheme:light){:root{--bg:#f5f8ff;--surface:#fff;--raised:#eef2fb;--border:#c9d3e6;--text:#0b1430;--muted:#4a5878;--ok:#1e7a4a;--bad:#b3261e}}\n*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;padding:16px;background:var(--bg);color:var(--text);font:14px/1.5 system-ui,sans-serif}\n.panel{background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:16px;padding:16px;margin:0 0 16px;max-width:760px}\nh2{margin:0 0 8px;font-size:16px}p{margin:0 0 8px}.note{color:var(--muted);font-size:12px}\nbutton,select,input{height:36px;padding:0 12px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:8px;background:var(--raised);color:inherit;font:inherit}\nbutton{cursor:pointer}button.primary{background:var(--action);border-color:var(--action);color:#f5f8ff;font-weight:600}\n.row{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;align-items:center;margin:8px 0}\n.days label{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:4px;margin-right:8px}.days input{height:auto}\ntable{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse}td{padding:6px 4px;border-top:1px solid var(--border);vertical-align:middle}\n.ok{color:var(--ok)}.bad{color:var(--bad)}#msg{min-height:1.4em;font-size:12px}\n</style></head><body>\n<div class=\"panel\"><h2>Sleep timer</h2>\n<p id=\"sleep\" class=\"note\">Off.</p>\n<div class=\"row\"><button data-min=\"15\">15 min</button><button data-min=\"30\">30 min</button><button data-min=\"60\">1 h</button><button data-min=\"90\">1 h 30</button><button id=\"cancel\">Cancel</button></div></div>\n\n<div class=\"panel\"><h2>Schedule</h2>\n<table id=\"rules\"></table>\n<p id=\"empty\" class=\"note\">No rules yet.</p>\n<h2 style=\"margin-top:12px\">Add a rule</h2>\n<div class=\"row days\" id=\"days\"></div>\n<div class=\"row\"><input id=\"time\" type=\"time\" value=\"23:30\" aria-label=\"Time\">\n<select id=\"action\"><option value=\"off\">Turn the TV off</option><option value=\"launch\">Open an app</option></select>\n<select id=\"app\" hidden aria-label=\"App\"><option value=\"\">Loading apps…</option></select>\n<button id=\"add\" class=\"primary\">Add</button><button id=\"test\">Test now</button></div>\n<p id=\"msg\" aria-live=\"polite\"></p>\n<p class=\"note\">Times are the TV's local time (<span id=\"tz\"></span>). A rule runs once a day, within two minutes of its time, and only while the TV is on: a time missed while it is off is skipped. Opening an app needs the TV on. Rules run while this Shard is switched on.</p></div>\n\n<div class=\"panel\"><h2>Last actions</h2><table id=\"log\"></table><p id=\"nolog\" class=\"note\">Nothing yet.</p></div>\n\n<div class=\"panel\"><h2>Reset</h2><p class=\"note\">Deletes every rule, cancels the sleep timer and clears the last actions, as after a fresh install.</p>\n<div class=\"row\"><button id=\"reset\">Reset Bedtime</button></div></div>\n<script>\nvar data=null,DAYS=['Sun','Mon','Tue','Wed','Thu','Fri','Sat'],ORDER=[1,2,3,4,5,6,0],appNames={};\nfunction $(id){return document.getElementById(id)}\nfunction api(u,b){return fetch(u,b===undefined?{}:{method:'POST',headers:{'Content-Type':'application/json'},body:JSON.stringify(b)}).then(function(r){return r.json().catch(function(){throw new Error('no answer from the Shard: open the Bedtime tab again')}).then(function(d){if(!r.ok||d.ok===false)throw new Error(d.error||'Action failed');return d})},function(){throw new Error('no answer from the Shard: open the Bedtime tab again')})}\nfunction say(t,bad){$('msg').textContent=t||'';$('msg').className=bad?'bad':''}\nfunction text(el,t){el.textContent=t;return el}\nfunction el(tag,t,cls){var e=document.createElement(tag);if(t!=null)e.textContent=t;if(cls)e.className=cls;return e}\nfunction when(ms){if(!ms)return '—';var d=new Date(ms);return DAYS[d.getDay()]+' '+('0'+d.getHours()).slice(-2)+':'+('0'+d.getMinutes()).slice(-2)}\nfunction what(r){return r.action==='off'?'Turn the TV off':'Open '+(r.appName||appNames[r.appId]||r.appId)}\nfunction daysText(days){if(days.length===7)return 'Every day';if(days.join()==='1,2,3,4,5')return 'Weekdays';if(days.join()==='0,6')return 'Weekends';return ORDER.filter(function(d){return days.indexOf(d)>=0}).map(function(d){return DAYS[d]}).join(' ')}\nfunction show(d){data=d;var off=-d.tzOffsetMinutes;$('tz').textContent='UTC'+(d.tzOffsetMinutes>=0?'+':'-')+Math.abs(d.tzOffsetMinutes/60);\n $('sleep').textContent=d.sleepAt?'The TV turns off at '+when(d.sleepAt).slice(4)+' ('+Math.max(1,Math.round((d.sleepAt-d.now)/60000))+' min).':'Off.';\n var t=$('rules');t.textContent='';$('empty').hidden=d.rules.length>0;\n d.rules.forEach(function(r,i){var tr=el('tr');\n  var on=document.createElement('input');on.type='checkbox';on.checked=r.enabled;on.title='Enabled';on.onchange=function(){var l=copy();l[i].enabled=this.checked;saveRules(l,this.checked?'Rule on.':'Rule off.')};\n  var td=el('td');td.appendChild(on);tr.appendChild(td);\n  tr.appendChild(el('td',r.time+' · '+daysText(r.days)));tr.appendChild(el('td',what(r)));tr.appendChild(el('td',r.enabled?'next '+when(r.next):'off','note'));\n  var del=el('button','Remove');del.onclick=function(){var l=copy();l.splice(i,1);saveRules(l,'Rule removed.')};td=el('td');td.appendChild(del);tr.appendChild(td);t.appendChild(tr)});\n var g=$('log');g.textContent='';$('nolog').hidden=d.log.length>0;\n d.log.forEach(function(x){var tr=el('tr');tr.appendChild(el('td',new Date(x.at).toLocaleString()));tr.appendChild(el('td',x.why));\n  tr.appendChild(el('td',x.action==='off'?'TV off':'Open '+(appNames[x.appId]||x.appId)));tr.appendChild(el('td',x.ok?'done':'failed: '+(x.error||''),x.ok?'ok':'bad'));g.appendChild(tr)})}\nfunction copy(){return data.rules.map(function(r){var o={id:r.id,enabled:r.enabled,time:r.time,days:r.days.slice(),action:r.action};if(r.appId){o.appId=r.appId;o.appName=r.appName}return o})}\nfunction saveRules(list,ok){return api('rules',{rules:list}).then(function(d){show(d);say(ok)}).catch(function(e){say(e.message,true);load()})}\nfunction load(){return api('state').then(show).catch(function(e){say(e.message,true)})}\nfunction picked(){var r={action:$('action').value};if(r.action==='launch'){r.appId=$('app').value;r.appName=appNames[r.appId]||''}return r}\nORDER.forEach(function(d){var l=el('label'),c=document.createElement('input');c.type='checkbox';c.value=d;c.checked=d>=0;l.appendChild(c);l.appendChild(document.createTextNode(DAYS[d]));$('days').appendChild(l)});\n$('action').onchange=function(){$('app').hidden=this.value!=='launch';if(this.value==='launch'&&!$('app').options[0].value)loadApps()};\nfunction loadApps(){api('apps').then(function(d){var s=$('app');s.textContent='';d.apps.forEach(function(a){appNames[a.appId]=a.name;var o=el('option',a.name);o.value=a.appId;s.appendChild(o)});if(data)show(data)}).catch(function(e){$('app').options[0].textContent='Apps unavailable: '+e.message})}\n$('add').onclick=function(){var days=[].slice.call(document.querySelectorAll('#days input')).filter(function(c){return c.checked}).map(function(c){return Number(c.value)});\n var r=picked();r.time=$('time').value;r.days=days;r.enabled=true;if(r.action==='launch'&&!r.appId){say('Pick an app',true);return}saveRules(copy().concat([r]),'Rule added.')};\n// The page runs in a sandbox without dialogs (confirm() would just return false): a second click confirms instead.\nvar armed=null;\n$('test').onclick=function(){var r=picked(),b=this;if(r.action==='launch'&&!r.appId){say('Pick an app',true);return}\n if(r.action==='off'&&!armed){armed=setTimeout(function(){armed=null;b.textContent='Test now'},5000);b.textContent='Click again: TV off';return}\n clearTimeout(armed);armed=null;b.textContent='Test now';say('Running…');api('run',r).then(function(d){show(d.state);say('Done.')}).catch(function(e){say(e.message,true);load()})};\n[].forEach.call(document.querySelectorAll('[data-min]'),function(b){b.onclick=function(){api('sleep',{minutes:Number(b.getAttribute('data-min'))}).then(function(d){show(d);say('Sleep timer set.')}).catch(function(e){say(e.message,true)})}});\n$('cancel').onclick=function(){api('sleep',{minutes:null}).then(function(d){show(d);say('Sleep timer cancelled.')}).catch(function(e){say(e.message,true)})};\nvar resetArmed=null;\n$('reset').onclick=function(){var b=this;if(!resetArmed){b.textContent='Click again: delete all rules';resetArmed=setTimeout(function(){resetArmed=null;b.textContent='Reset Bedtime'},5000);return}\n clearTimeout(resetArmed);resetArmed=null;b.textContent='Reset Bedtime';api('reset',{}).then(function(d){show(d);say('Reset done: no rules, no sleep timer.')}).catch(function(e){say(e.message,true)})};\nload();setInterval(load,30000);\n</script></body></html>\n"}}
